<p>
Additional notes:
</p>

<ul class="org-ul">
<li><a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs#navigation-substitution">Substitution</a>: I use <code>(add-hook 'substitute-post-replace-functions #'sacha-substitute-save-common-edits)</code> to save the changes. <a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs#navigation-substitution">sacha-substitute-save-common-edits</a>
<a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs#edit-text">Edit text</a> has functions like <code>sacha-subed-fix-common-errors-in-text</code> that apply those changes to my speech recognition results and <code>sacha-subed-fix-common-errors-from-start</code> that apply them to already-prepared transcripts.</li>

<li><a href="https://github.com/sachac/whisper.el/">sachac/whisper.el</a> has my fork of <a href="https://github.com/natrys/whisper.el">natrys/whisper.el</a> to support voice commands. <a href="https://codeberg.org/sachac/speech-input">speech-input</a> has a bunch of other things, too, and of course <a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs/">my Emacs config</a>.</li>

<li>I've been using <a href="https://github.com/ErikPrantare/phony.el">phony</a> to define more voice commands using a parser.</li>

<li>Apparently I cannot spell when thinking out loud. It is <a href="https://www.orgzlyrevived.com/">Orgzly Revived</a>, not ogrzly.</li>

<li>This actually doesn't use generative AI in the sense of Gemini or Claude, except for the conversational French demo. I use a local speech recognition model (currently <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/10/clip-emacs-voice-control-describing-my-setup-during-linkarzu-s-livestream/emacsconf-subed.el">Orukeet</a>) and local speech synthesis (<a href="https://github.com/remsky/Kokoro-FastAPI">Kokoro FastAPI</a>), So depending on your feelings about large language models, the models might be small enough to be fine with you. Alternatively, there are classical approaches to both speech recognition and speech synthesis like <a href="https://kaldi-asr.org/">kaldi</a> and <a href="https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng">espeak-ng</a>.</li>
</ul>

